# On-Chip Activation Quantization Experiment

## Change

Moved FP32-to-Q8_0 activation quantization from the CPU into the FPGA. The accelerator reads FP32 activations from DRAM, quantizes each 32-element block into BRAM, and runs the existing GEMV datapath. Activation scales are stored as FP32 rather than GGML’s FP16.

Candidate source commit: `4a14a8729960bd3153a9deaaf40385bf7b086d3a`.

## Setup

Ultra96, FPGA clock approximately 100 MHz, Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct Q8_0, one CPU thread, context 512, 16 generated tokens, temperature 0, seed 1. Verification was disabled for timing. Each executable used its matching bitstream.

