An earlier two-token verification run completed successfully with 181 offloaded GEMVs and zero fallbacks. Against the CPU reference, maximum absolute error was `0.00552`; normalized maximum error was `0.000615` (0.0615%). Bit-exact rows were 0.01%.

## Conclusion

On-chip activation quantization functions on the board with zero CPU fallbacks. Backend time decreased by 0.091 s (approximately 0.25%), but both versions displayed 0.4 tok/s. This single run demonstrates no meaningful decode speedup. Output differences require further accuracy evaluation; backend timing alone excludes the golden path’s CPU quantization cost.
